Package: WaverideR
Type: Package
Title: Extracting Signals from Wavelet Spectra
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Michiel", family = "Arts", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "michiel.arts@stratigraphy.eu", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3181-4608"))
Maintainer: Michiel Arts <michiel.arts@stratigraphy.eu>
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: astrochron, graphics, grDevices, parallel, stats, utils
Suggests: knitr, magick, rmarkdown, scico, shiny, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Description: Extracts and analyses cyclic signals in stratigraphic and other
    time series using the continuous wavelet transform (Torrence and Compo
    (1998) <doi:10.1175/1520-0477(1998)079%3C0061:APGTWA%3E2.0.CO;2>),
    superlets (Moca et al. (2021) <doi:10.1038/s41467-020-20539-9>) and
    synchrosqueezed transforms (Daubechies et al. (2011)
    <doi:10.1016/j.acha.2010.08.002>), with significance tests, tracking of
    astronomical cycles and sedimentation rates, age models with uncertainty
    and de-chirped spectra. When using the package please cite both the paper
    that introduced it, Arts et al. (2024) <doi:10.3389/feart.2024.1357751>,
    and the package itself, Arts (2023)
    <https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=WaverideR>; see citation("WaverideR").
License: GPL (>= 2)
